-- allium: 3
-- federated-sharing.allium

-- Scope: Sharing and following selected pages from a sovereign Vera library
-- Includes: Delimited selections, individual and shared destinations,
--   read-only subscriptions, synchronised replicas, local editing, origin
--   review, provenance and withdrawal limits
-- Excludes:
--   - Authentication and grant mechanics (identity-access.allium)
--   - Conflict resolution between divergent copies
--   - Storage implementation
--   - Transport and instance identity between peers (peer-networking.allium)
-- Dependencies: Graph, Page and Participant are governed by core.allium; a
--   destination that is itself a sovereign Vera instance is named by its
--   stable identity from peer-networking.allium

use "./core.allium" as core
use "./peer-networking.allium" as peer

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Contracts
------------------------------------------------------------

contract SovereignSharing {
    share: (selection: SharedSelection, destination: SharingDestination) -> Distribution
    edit: (distribution: Distribution, author: core/Participant, page: core/Page) -> SharedEdit
    contribute: (distribution: Distribution, author: core/Participant, edits: List<SharedEdit>) -> Contribution
    review: (selection: ReviewSelection, owner: core/Participant, decision: ReviewDecision) -> ReviewOutcome
    withdraw: (distribution: Distribution) -> Withdrawal
    acknowledge_withdrawal: (withdrawal: Withdrawal, recipient: String, disposition: WithdrawalDisposition) -> WithdrawalAcknowledgement
    continue_after_withdrawal: (distribution: Distribution, custody: SharingDestination) -> ContinuationFork

    @invariant SharingIsDelimited
        -- Sharing a project or concept selects pages explicitly or by a visible
        -- criterion. It never grants the destination discovery of the remaining
        -- personal library merely because selected pages came from it.

    @invariant TheOriginAndHistoryTravel
        -- Every delivered page keeps a stable reference to its source library,
        -- source page and shared history. A synchronised copy does not pretend
        -- to be an unrelated page merely because it now lives elsewhere.

    @invariant OriginMeansWhereSharingBegan
        -- Origin is literally the personal library and page from which the
        -- sovereign participant first shared the resource. Synchronising,
        -- editing, accepting changes or sharing onward never transfers or
        -- rewrites that origin.

    @invariant HorizontalParticipationDoesNotEraseOrigin
        -- Participants with equivalent writing authority collaborate
        -- horizontally inside the granted relationship. Equality of permission
        -- does not make every replica an origin or remove the source owner's
        -- responsibility for the canonical history.

    @invariant AReceivedCopyEntersAnotherSovereignty
        -- A person, shared graph or site that synchronises content receives a
        -- replica under its custody. While sharing remains active, replicas point
        -- to the same logical page identity rather than becoming unrelated
        -- documents. After withdrawal, continued custody requires an explicit
        -- fork or another declared basis; an automatic cache is not by itself an
        -- independent work that may be retained indefinitely.

    @invariant AuthorisedEditorsDoNotWaitToWork
        -- A participant to whom the selection was shared with write authority
        -- changes their replica without prior approval. Their hand does not wait
        -- for the origin to be online or for its owner to review the difference.

    @invariant TheOriginReviewsWhatReturns
        -- A remote edit does not silently enter the source library's canonical
        -- page. Synchronisation presents the differences to the sovereign owner,
        -- who accepts or rejects them before they join the source history.

    @invariant AcceptanceAndRejectionStayAttributed
        -- Accepting records the remote author and the owner who accepted; it
        -- never reattributes the contribution to the owner. Rejecting preserves
        -- enough evidence to explain why replicas differ without adding the
        -- proposed content to the canonical page.

    @invariant AContributionArrivesAsACoherentBatch
        -- Changes produced together travel together with their author, order and
        -- dependencies. Synchronisation does not flatten them into unrelated
        -- prompts that make the intention of the contribution unrecoverable.

    @invariant ReviewCutsOnlyAtStructuralBoundaries
        -- The owner may review the complete contribution, a dependency-closed
        -- group or whole blocks. Vera never asks the owner to accept arbitrary
        -- lines or an operation whose required operations were rejected.

    @invariant PartialAcceptanceNeverInventsAnEdit
        -- Whatever is accepted consists of edits the remote participant actually
        -- submitted. Review can select coherent structural parts; it cannot
        -- silently synthesise prose or a block state written by neither person.

    @invariant UnsharingEndsTheRelationship
        -- The owner can stop future synchronisation and editing authority by
        -- withdrawing the distribution. This ends the relationship and asks
        -- every known recipient to stop serving and indexing its replica. It
        -- cannot erase observations or copies outside Vera's control.

    @invariant WithdrawalDoesNotEndOtherPeoplesWork
        -- A recipient may continue retained work after withdrawal as an editable
        -- fork under new canonical custody. The source owner can end the sharing
        -- relationship, not prohibit independent continuation of what was
        -- already distributed.

    @invariant ContinuationIsNewAndItsDerivationIsPermanent
        -- The continuing fork receives a new identity and canonical history. It
        -- permanently names the withdrawn distribution and original pages as
        -- its derivation; it never presents itself as the still-synchronised
        -- original or rewrites where sharing began.

    @invariant PendingWorkSurvivesTheCut
        -- Remote edits not yet reviewed when withdrawal occurs remain explicit
        -- in the continuing fork or are deliberately discarded by its new
        -- custodian. Withdrawal never makes pending work vanish silently.

    @invariant ASharedSpaceContinuesTogether
        -- When the withdrawn destination was one shared graph or shared site,
        -- its normal continuation is one common fork governed by that space.
        -- Withdrawal does not automatically create one fork per participant;
        -- a participant may establish a separate fork only by an explicit later
        -- decision.

    @invariant ASharedSpaceHasAnOriginalHumanCustodian
        -- A shared graph or site is constituted and sponsored by a human who
        -- supplies its original custody, even when collaboration inside it is
        -- horizontal. Collective governance does not make the infrastructure
        -- ownerless or hide who remains responsible if the group cannot act.

    @invariant TheAuthorisedGroupGovernsBeforeTheFallbackOwner
        -- When a participant withdraws a contribution from a shared space, the
        -- participants who retain governing authority over that space govern
        -- its common continuation. If that group cannot exercise custody, the
        -- space's original owner is the explicit fallback; the withdrawn
        -- contribution's origin does not regain control merely by withdrawing.

    @invariant WithdrawalStopsTheFutureNotThePast
        -- Withdrawing stops future discovery and synchronisation from the source
        -- and propagates a retraction to every known recipient. A recipient
        -- controlled by the federation stops serving and indexing its cached
        -- replica immediately, then either purges it or declares the independent
        -- basis on which it retains a continuation. Vera does not report a copy
        -- erased without that recipient's acknowledgement.

    @invariant WithdrawalAndPersonalDataErasureAreDifferentActs
        -- An author may withdraw a distribution while keeping the source page in
        -- their sovereign corpus. A personal-data erasure request concerns the
        -- continued treatment of identified personal data and may require their
        -- deletion or anonymisation in the source as well as recipient replicas.
        -- Neither act silently implies the other.

    @invariant VoluntaryPublicationIsNotPerpetualConsent
        -- Sharing data deliberately makes its prior distribution legitimate; it
        -- does not grant recipients an irrevocable right to keep processing it.
        -- A recipient that retains or republishes after retraction acts under its
        -- own declared responsibility rather than the withdrawn permission.

    @invariant FederationCachesHonourRetraction
        -- Storage maintained only to deliver or synchronise an active
        -- distribution is a cache, not a continuation fork. Retraction removes
        -- that content from reading, search and discovery immediately and the
        -- recipient purges it according to the federation's bounded policy.

    @invariant IrreversibilityIsKnownBeforeSharing
        -- Before the first distribution, Vera tells the sovereign participant
        -- that recipients may retain synchronised copies and that public access
        -- can be observed or copied beyond Vera's control.
}

contract SovereignSubscription {
    follow: (selection: SharedSelection, subscriber: SharingDestination) -> SurfaceSubscription
    refresh: (subscription: SurfaceSubscription, observed_revision: String) -> SurfaceSubscription
    stop: (subscription: SurfaceSubscription) -> SurfaceSubscription

    @invariant FollowingIsReadOnlyAtTheSource
        -- Following a surface receives revisions and provenance without granting
        -- authority to change the source. A later contribution or collaboration
        -- requires its own explicit sharing relationship and grant.

    @invariant TheSourceRemainsCanonical
        -- A subscribed copy always names the source graph and source pages as
        -- canonical. Caching, indexing or annotating the copy never promotes the
        -- subscriber into an origin or a second source of truth.

    @invariant LocalAnnotationsRemainLocal
        -- Notes, links and classifications made around a subscribed copy belong
        -- to the subscriber's Vera. They do not travel back to the source or to
        -- other subscribers unless deliberately contributed through another
        -- governed relationship.

    @invariant FreshnessIsVisible
        -- A reader can tell which source revision was last observed and when the
        -- subscription last checked. An unavailable source produces visible
        -- staleness rather than presenting a cached copy as current.

    @invariant SubscriptionDoesNotDelegateRedistribution
        -- Receiving a surface does not grant authority to offer that surface to
        -- third parties. Republishing requires a separate permission or an
        -- explicit continuation whose derivation and new custody remain visible.

    @invariant StoppingFollowDoesNotEraseLocalWork
        -- Stopping a subscription ends future refreshes. It does not silently
        -- delete local annotations; retaining the source content itself requires
        -- an allowed cache, an explicit import or a declared continuation fork.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

enum DestinationKind { participant | participants | shared_graph | shared_site | public }
enum DistributionStatus { offered | synchronised | withdrawn }
enum ContributionStatus { local | awaiting_review | partially_reviewed | accepted | rejected }
enum ReviewDecision { accept | reject }
enum ReviewBoundary { whole_contribution | dependent_group | whole_block }
enum WithdrawalDisposition { purged | continued_independently | unable_to_confirm }
enum SubscriptionStatus { active | stopped }

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Values
------------------------------------------------------------

entity SharedSelection {
    source: core/Graph
    pages: List<core/Page>
    criterion: String?
    selected_by: core/Participant
}

entity SharingDestination {
    kind: DestinationKind
    address: String
    -- Set only when this destination is itself a sovereign Vera instance
    -- reached over the horizontal peer network; its stable identity, not a
    -- mutable address, is what a Distribution actually travels to.
    peer_identity: peer/PeerIdentity?
    original_owner: core/Participant?
    governors: List<core/Participant>
}

entity Distribution {
    selection: SharedSelection
    destination: SharingDestination
    status: DistributionStatus
    shared_at: Timestamp
    withdrawal: Withdrawal?
    edits: SharedEdit with distribution = this
    contributions: Contribution with distribution = this
    continuations: ContinuationFork with withdrawn_distribution = this
}

entity SurfaceSubscription {
    selection: SharedSelection
    subscriber: SharingDestination
    status: SubscriptionStatus
    observed_revision: String?
    last_checked_at: Timestamp?
}

entity Withdrawal {
    distribution: Distribution
    requested_at: Timestamp
    acknowledgements: WithdrawalAcknowledgement with withdrawal = this
}

entity WithdrawalAcknowledgement {
    withdrawal: Withdrawal
    recipient: String
    disposition: WithdrawalDisposition
    independent_basis: String?
    acknowledged_at: Timestamp
}

entity SharedEdit {
    distribution: Distribution
    page: core/Page
    author: core/Participant
    recorded_at: Timestamp
}

entity Contribution {
    distribution: Distribution
    author: core/Participant
    edits: List<SharedEdit>
    status: ContributionStatus
    submitted_at: Timestamp
    reviews: ReviewOutcome with contribution = this
}

entity ReviewSelection {
    contribution: Contribution
    boundary: ReviewBoundary
    edits: List<SharedEdit>
}

entity ReviewOutcome {
    contribution: Contribution
    selection: ReviewSelection
    reviewer: core/Participant
    decision: ReviewDecision
    reviewed_at: Timestamp
}

entity ContinuationFork {
    withdrawn_distribution: Distribution
    canonical_custody: SharingDestination
    derived_from: List<core/Page>
    created_at: Timestamp
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

invariant ASelectionNeverEscapesItsSourceGraph {
    for selection in SharedSelections:
        selection.pages.all(page => page in selection.source.pages)
}

invariant AWithdrawalNamesAWithdrawnDistribution {
    for withdrawal in Withdrawals:
        withdrawal.distribution.status = withdrawn
}

invariant IndependentRetentionDeclaresItsBasis {
    for acknowledgement in WithdrawalAcknowledgements:
        acknowledgement.disposition = continued_independently
            implies acknowledgement.independent_basis != null
}

invariant PurgingDoesNotClaimIndependentCustody {
    for acknowledgement in WithdrawalAcknowledgements:
        acknowledgement.disposition = purged
            implies acknowledgement.independent_basis = null
}

invariant ASharedEditBelongsToTheSharedSelection {
    for edit in SharedEdits:
        edit.page in edit.distribution.selection.pages
}

invariant AReviewSelectsOnlySubmittedEdits {
    for selection in ReviewSelections:
        selection.edits.all(edit => edit in selection.contribution.edits)
}

invariant AContinuationComesFromAWithdrawnDistribution {
    for fork in ContinuationForks:
        fork.withdrawn_distribution.status = withdrawn
}

invariant ASharedSpaceHasAtMostOneCommonContinuation {
    for a in ContinuationForks:
        for b in ContinuationForks:
            a != b
                and a.withdrawn_distribution = b.withdrawn_distribution
                and a.withdrawn_distribution.destination.kind in {shared_graph, shared_site}
                implies a.canonical_custody != b.canonical_custody
}

invariant EverySharedSpaceHasAFallbackOwner {
    for destination in SharingDestinations:
        destination.kind in {shared_graph, shared_site}
            implies destination.original_owner != null
}

invariant EverySubscriptionFollowsOneSovereignSelection {
    for subscription in SurfaceSubscriptions:
        subscription.selection.pages.all(page => page in subscription.selection.source.pages)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Answered: an authorised participant edits their replica directly; the source
-- owner accepts or rejects the differences when they return.
-- Answered: differences arrive as one coherent contribution. Review may accept
-- the whole contribution, dependency-closed groups or whole blocks, never
-- arbitrary lines or dependency-breaking operations.
open question "When a shared selection criterion gains or loses a page, does synchronisation follow the criterion automatically or require a new sharing decision?"
-- Answered in part: every known recipient returns a disposition saying that it
-- purged the cache, continued independently under a declared basis, or could not
-- confirm the result. Vera never infers erasure from silence.
open question "How long is withdrawal acknowledgement evidence retained, and what identifying detail may it contain without recreating the personal data that was purged?"
open question "What bounded purge period applies to an acknowledged federated cache after it has stopped serving and indexing withdrawn content?"
open question "Which authority decides whether a recipient's declared independent basis permits retention after a personal-data erasure request?"
open question "Can a public destination synchronise canonical page identity, or does it receive only a publication projection?"
open question "Does a Distribution to a federated peer travel as one peer-networking SharedScope per shared selection, and how does the selection's explicit page list correspond to SharedScope's opaque scope_id?"
open question "What signed and versioned manifest lets a subscriber verify membership, revisions, attachments, provenance and retractions without learning anything outside the selected surface?"
open question "May a subscriber pin an older source revision after a newer one appears, and how does the interface distinguish intentional pinning from accidental staleness?"
open question "When local annotations cite a page that later leaves the source selection, what minimal tombstone may remain without leaking withdrawn content?"
open question "Which institutional records may accept direct remote edits, which accept only attributed proposals, and which fields remain authoritative in a participant's personal Vera?"
open question "For a medical surface, how do consent withdrawal, clinical correction, emergency access and legally required retention coexist without pretending that either the patient or the clinician owns the entire record?"
-- Answered: recipients may continue as an editable fork with new identity and
-- canonical custody, permanently derived from the immutable historical origin.
-- Answered: a shared graph or site normally continues as one common fork under
-- that space's custody. Separate participant forks require explicit decisions.
-- Answered: the authorised group governs that common continuation; if it cannot
-- act, custody falls back to the shared space's original human owner.
